#: ../../../gpu/xe/xe_gt_stats.rst:5
msgid "Xe GT Statistics"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/xe/xe_gt_stats:7: ../drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_gt_stats.c:16
msgid ""
"The Xe driver exposes per-GT statistics through the debugfs filesystem at::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/xe/xe_gt_stats:7: ../drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_gt_stats.c:20
msgid ""
"This interface requires the kernel to be built with ``CONFIG_DEBUG_FS=y``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/xe/xe_gt_stats:7: ../drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_gt_stats.c:25
msgid ""
"Reading the file prints all available statistics, one per line, in ``name: "
"value`` format::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/xe/xe_gt_stats:7: ../drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_gt_stats.c:33
msgid ""
"All values are 64-bit unsigned integers aggregated across all CPUs. Counters "
"accumulate since the driver was loaded or since the last explicit reset.  "
"Timing counters use microseconds as their unit; data volume counters use KiB."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/xe/xe_gt_stats:7: ../drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_gt_stats.c:41
msgid "Writing a boolean true value to the file resets all counters to zero::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu/xe/xe_gt_stats:7: ../drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_gt_stats.c:45
msgid ""
"Any value accepted by ``kstrtobool()`` (e.g. ``1``, ``y``, ``yes``, ``on``) "
"triggers the reset.  Resetting while the GPU is active may yield "
"unpredictable intermediate values; it is recommended to reset only when the "
"GPU is idle."
msgstr ""

